WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.934
Joining us

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:01.534
right now is

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.202
former NATO

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.403
supreme allied commander

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:05.071
and CNN military analyst

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:05.972
General Wesley Clark.

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:06.539
It's good to see you.

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:07.207
General, let's start

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:10.143
with kind of exactly what John and Sam

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.211
Kiley were talking about.

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:13.346
We have these latest

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:14.814
and continued

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.617
strikes day and night coming from Russia

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:18.718
into Ukraine.

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:20.153
But now we are at the same time

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:22.322
we're seeing more and more strikes

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.923
on Russian soil.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.792
What does this intensity is

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:26.292
kind of the way

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.660
I'm kind of describing in this moment

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.328
suggest to you

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:31.531
about this phase of the war

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:34.200
Russia still doesn't

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.602
have the means to really go

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:37.470
after significant

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.572
Ukrainian military targets

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:40.673
with its missiles.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:42.675
For whatever reason, it just doesn't.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:43.543
And it feels

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:45.111
it gets better return

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.414
by simply punishing the Ukrainian people.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:49.682
It's like if you're not

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:51.017
if you don't like me,

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.318
I'm going to kill you.

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:55.088
And so it's a personal attack

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:57.524
by the Russians on the Ukrainian people.

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:59.692
Iranians, on the other hand, recognize

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:02.762
that Belgorod is a key logistics center.

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:05.398
So these additional Russian forces

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.332
that are moving in around

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.501
Belgorod are actually disrupting

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.637
the ability of the Russian forces

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:11.371
to respond

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.405
to a potential

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.407
Ukrainian counteroffensive.

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:16.876
Now, where that counteroffensive is,

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:19.579
we don't know, could be in the mood area.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.681
It could be in the south toward multiple

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:23.283
It could be in the north

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.751
northeast of Clark.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.086
And in that case,

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:27.787
what happens in Belgorod

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:30.123
would be really significant.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.125
The Ukrainians are not disclosing this,

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:33.159
and they probably haven't

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.661
even made a decision on it.

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:35.628
A lot of it depends.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:36.763
This is a cat and mouse

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:37.997
game at this point.

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.866
They're doing reconnaissance in force

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:41.067
or using their artillery

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.902
they're looking at Russian reactions

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:43.870
and they're trying to assess

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.972
where their best opportunities are.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.407
And I wanted to ask you about that.

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:49.008
But in terms of a best opportunity,

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:49.642
because we have heard

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:50.143
so much

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:52.979
about the imminent counter offensive,

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:54.647
and when it comes down to

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:55.782
if you want to call these

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.784
the final moments before it would begin.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.619
What are the right conditions

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:00.620
in your view, General?

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.155
For Ukraine to launch this effort?

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:05.492
First of

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:06.626
all, you've got to

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.028
look at the environmental situation on

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:12.532
the ground going to support your forces.

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:15.001
Secondly, you've got to look at where

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:15.735
the Russians are,

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:16.669
the Russian strengths,

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:18.471
weaknesses, dispositions.

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:18.905
And third,

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:20.473
you've got to look at your own forces

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.474
and where they are

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:22.242
or they're ready

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:23.143
is all the equipment

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:25.411
there Is there more training to be done?

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:28.281
And then you have to put these conditions

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:30.450
under a plan that works.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.285
That plan is going to involve

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:33.887
some deception

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:36.089
It's going to involve some French.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:38.124
We're going to be surprised by it.

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:38.925
So we

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:39.926
and the American side,

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.327
not only the American public,

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:43.296
but probably the American military

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:44.864
don't really know

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:47.467
what the Ukrainians will actually do.

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.035
There have been some wargaming

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:50.203
or some cooperation there.

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:51.838
There's obviously intelligence

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:53.540
sharing on both sides.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.575
But the actual command decisions,

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:56.409
those are going to be held

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.211
very close by Ukraine.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:00.213
We are moving into the period

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:02.215
where the ground is drawing out.

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:04.584
We are getting a lot more

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:05.885
Western equipment

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:06.753
in and the training

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:09.088
is continuing for the Ukrainian forces.

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:10.623
Question is, is.

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.592
What's the Russian disposition?

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:14.027
Where are the weaknesses?

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:15.528
What about that

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:16.229
in place

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:17.297
and what mood

00:03:17.297 --> 00:03:19.465
is that going to provide an opportunity?

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:21.868
Where do they stand in the south

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:22.769
and the Ukrainians

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:25.104
actually get to the Crimea land bridge

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:26.906
if they can?

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:27.874
That's decisive

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:31.344
because this war only ends when Mr.

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:33.379
Putin realizes he's going to lose.

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:34.681
That's why,

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:35.815
although the United States

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:38.151
is not encouraging and supporting it,

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:40.153
these Ukrainian attacks into Russia,

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:42.055
even the drones in Moscow

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:44.190
are strategically valuable.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.725
They bring the fact home

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:46.793
to the Russian people that,

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:47.894
yes, there's a war.

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:49.395
It's not a police action.

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:51.364
And yes, the Ukrainians are real people

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:52.899
and they are going to fight back.

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:55.034
And you need to stop this.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:57.070
So this is all part

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:58.938
of the strategic build.

00:03:58.938 --> 00:03:59.672
So I think

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.741
we're going to have a very busy summer.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.876
But we can't predict where or when.

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:05.144
You think

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:06.646
it's great to have you on, as always.

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:07.814
General, thank you for your time.

